~ start
do stage_party("Jayce", "base")
if Flags.get_level_flag("jayce_date_hint_given") == true:
	=> lab_access_again
elif Flags.get_level_flag("jayce_introduced") == true:
	Jayce: Back again, sweetheart?
else
	A man in a grey work jacket leans against the wall, arms folded, watching the corridor.
	He's looking at you and Layla like a hyena looking at an unattended picnic.
=> hub

~ hub
What do you want to say to him?
- Who are you?
	=> who_are_you
- We can't enter the lab. [Proceed] [if Flags.get_level_flag("lab_keypad_interacted") == true and Flags.get_level_flag("jayce_introduced") == true]
	=> lab_access
- Nothing. Never mind. [Leave]
	=> leave

~ who_are_you
Player: Hey. Do you mind telling us who you are?
You notice him straightening up. He wasn't expecting to be spoken to first.
Jayce: Me? Course not, sweetheart.
Jayce: Name's Jayce. Work is Maintenance.
do Flags.set_level_flag("jayce_introduced", true)
Jayce: And what do I owe the pleasure?
Player: I'm Fiona, and this is Layla. We work here, in the genomics lab.
Player: First time I've seen you around.
Jayce: Wouldn't have. I only do nights.
Jayce: You lot don't turn up till ten most days.
Player: Fair enough.
Player: I usually take my late nights in the library instead of the lab. Unless I absolutely need to be here.
if Flags.get_level_flag("party_companion_staged") == true:
	Layla: Which you shouldn't be doing at all!
	Layla: Nights are for rest and recovery!
	Player: Yeah, yeah. I know.
	He watches the two of you for a beat longer than the exchange warrants.
	Jayce: Aww, what a bunch of lovebirds y'all are.
	Jayce: How 'bout a sleepover, huh? Bet you girls do those all the time.
	Jayce: Bet it smells nice in there in the sheets with you two.
	Layla: ...Sorry?
	Jayce: Oh, don't mind it, sweetheart.
	Jayce: It's just that looking at how much you care for each other has gotten me a lil' bit...
	Jayce: Excited.
	#Fiona turns to Layla
	do party_huddle()
	Layla: Fiona! This man is hella creepy! Let's get away from him!
	Player: Don't worry. People like him can be made useful.
	Layla: What do you mean?
	Player: Don't know yet. But you'll see soon.
	if Flags.get_game_counter("layla_closeness") < 0:
		Layla: ...If you say so.
	else
		Layla: Hmm. If you say so, Fiona.
	do party_unhuddle()
	Jayce: What are you two hot things whisperin' about?
	Player: Nothing you need to worry about.
Jayce: Anyway. I'll let you get back to it.
Jayce: You know where to find me.
Player: Sure.
=> hub

~ lab_access
if Flags.get_level_flag("jayce_date_hint_given") == true:
	=> lab_access_again
Player: Hey. As maintenance, you must have access to all the rooms in this building, right?
Jayce: Sure do. Got my keycard right here.
He whips a keycard out of his front pocket.
Jayce: Can get into any darn room with this thing.
Jayce: Well... most of 'em. Keypad rooms, not so much.
Jayce: Why? Wanna break into some place you're not supposed to be, sugar?
Player: Not really. We want to get into our own lab. But the password seems to have been changed.
Jayce: Huh? Has it? It was the same yesterday.
Jayce: Good ol' freedom day. Seen ya professor punch it in a hundred times.
Player: That's what we tried, but it doesn't seem to work now.
Player: And we've got urgent work that needs to be done in there.
Jayce: Well, too damn bad, sweetie. Looks like it can't be helped.
Jayce: The keypad enforces a password change once every year.
Jayce: Suppose it was yesterday it asked for one, and ya professor obliged.
Jayce: And my card don't do nothin' for it.
if Flags.get_level_flag("party_companion_staged") == true:
	do actor_effect("Layla", "jump")
	Layla: No way!
	do actor_effect("Layla", "tremble")
	Layla: Fiona! What should we do now?
	if Flags.get_game_counter("layla_closeness") >= 0:
		Layla: Should I let go of my goals?
		Layla: Do I belong in the streets?
		Player: No.
		Player: I mean, I don't know. But probably not?
Player: There's gotta be something we can do still.
Player: So hey, Jayce. Jayce it was, right?
Player: Jayce, can you tell us anything about the previous passwords?
Player: You know, before this one?
Player: Maybe there's a pattern here we can uncover.
Jayce: Well, babe, I been here three years.
Jayce: And while I don't remember no old passwords digit by digit...
Jayce: I do remember all of 'em been some kind of a date.
Jayce: Easier for your professor to remember, I reckon.
if Flags.get_level_flag("party_companion_staged") == true:
	Layla: That's true.
	Layla: I've noticed the professor randomly drops dates into conversation.
	Layla: He's definitely a nerd that way.
Player: I see...
Player: If... if all his previous passwords have been dates...
Player: It IS likely the new one is too.
if Flags.get_level_flag("party_companion_staged") == true:
	Layla: But what could it be, Fiona?
Player: Not sure. We'll have to look around. There might be clues here.
Jayce: Love the go-getter attitude. It's hot on ya, blondie.
Jayce: Tell ol' Jayce one thing, though. Why not just call ya professor and ask him for it?
do Flags.set_level_flag("jayce_date_hint_given", true)
if Flags.get_level_flag("party_companion_staged") == true:
	do actor_effect("Layla", "slump")
	Layla: Well, we could do that...
	do actor_effect("Layla", "tremble")
	Layla: But I'd rather not.
	Layla: I don't even want him thinking for a second I got the sequencing done today.
	Layla: According to him, it was done days ago!
	Jayce: I'll sequence you if you lemme, girl.
	do actor_effect("Layla", "shock")
	Layla: OH. MY. GOD. Shut up!
	Player: It's alright. Never mind, Jayce. We'll look around and see what we can do.
	Jayce: Sure thing. All the best, blondie and brownie.
	do party_huddle()
	Layla: So, I hate him.
	Player: I know, but let's keep it cool with him.
	Player: Never know if he could turn out helpful.
	do actor_effect("Layla", "slump")
	if Flags.get_game_counter("layla_closeness") < 0:
		Layla: Fine.
	else
		Layla: Ugh. Okay, Fiona. I'll try.
		Layla: But only because you insist!
	Player: Thanks, Layla.
	Player: Anyway. We should look for clues. Stuff around the building. Anything that pertains to Professor Greene.
	Player: And can lead us to a date.
	Layla: Alright, let's do this!
	Player: I'm letting you know this, though. It's probably a long shot.
	Player: He may not have even set a date as the passcode.
	if Flags.get_game_counter("layla_closeness") >= 0:
		Player: I would rate our chances of success at approximately...
		Player: Nine and a half percent!
		do actor_effect("Layla", "jump")
		Layla: NINE AND A HALF!
		Layla: So precise! I bet you used some complicated formula in your mind to come to that number!
		Player: Yeah.
		Player: (I pulled that outta my ass. She takes everything I say at face value.)
		Layla: Regardless, I'll take those chances.
		Layla: It's all that I can do right now!
		Layla: Put my trust in my prodigious mentor!
		Player: Yeah, yeah.
	else
		Layla: Then we'd better start.
	Player: Anyway, let's go.
	do party_unhuddle()
	=> END

else
	# step 2.227: no solo playthrough (Layla is always with Fiona). fallback only, so the branch stays valid.
	Player: This is a template line.
	=> END

~ lab_access_again
Jayce: Still locked out, huh, blondie?
Player: Working on it.
=> jayce_return_hub

~ jayce_return_hub
What do you want to ask him?
- Ask him about his life.
	=> jayce_life
- Ask him where you should look.
	=> jayce_where_to_look
- That's all. [Leave]
	=> leave

~ jayce_life
Player: So, Jayce. How long have you been mopping these halls?
Jayce: Long enough to know which doors stick, sugar.
Jayce: Nights mostly. Quiet.
Jayce: Nobody there to watch the watcher.
Player: Hmm. That's... comforting.
if Flags.get_level_flag("party_companion_staged") == true:
	Behind you, Layla winces.
=> jayce_return_hub

~ jayce_where_to_look
do Flags.set_level_flag("jayce_pointed_to_biochem", true)
Player: If you were us, where would you start looking?
Jayce: Dunno, sugar. But since ya can't call the man himself...
Jayce: Ain't there any other of y'all lil science nerds working in your lab who could help ya?
Player: Not really. It's just us who work in this lab.
Player: Well, apart from the professor himself, obviously.
if Flags.get_level_flag("party_companion_staged") == true:
	do party_huddle()
	Layla: Fiona, what about someone from the Biochem lab?
	Layla: I imagine the departments cross-collaborate a lot, don't they?
	Layla: Surely someone from there must know something, right?
	Player: Well, there's one guy from that department who's entered our lab multiple times to talk to Professor Greene.
	Player: He doesn't usually come around at this hour.
	Player: And anyway, he visits us infrequently.
	Player: Not a high chance he was in here yesterday evening.
	Layla: Oh. I see.
	Player: Regardless, if he is around, I suppose we could ask him about it.
	Player: Even though I'd rather not.
	Layla: You'll see.
	do party_unhuddle()
	Jayce: Well, glad I could help you ladies with that.
else
	# step 2.227: no solo playthrough (Layla is always with Fiona). fallback only, so the branch stays valid.
	Player: This is a template line.
Player: Right. Thanks.
=> jayce_return_hub

~ leave
Jayce: Suit yourself.
=> END
